            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 30 changed paths for security, authorization, data-loss and unsafe-input risk; no reachable exploit found.",
              "engine/runtime/pi_agents.go keeps the existing ownership proof: a link is touched only when readlink matches the package path. Conflicting files or foreign symlinks are left untouched on install and uninstall, and a failure on one agent does not stop the others. File names come from a directory listing, so path traversal is not reachable.",
              "engine/pipkg/build.go copyPiAgents copies only top-level .md files from the overlay's own pi/agents into the package. It reads from an owner-controlled tree and uses the existing copyFile helper, so no new untrusted-input path is added.",
              "engine/skills/routes.go codex-agent route mirrors the existing opencode-agent route. Rows outside codex/agents/ are non-deployable, and a missing agents root is refused. Manifest rows are owner-controlled, so it adds no new trust boundary.",
              "No secrets, dependency or lockfile changes are present in the candidate."
            ]
          }
