              {
                "id": "R4-unlink-needs-package-dir",
                "lens": "resilience",
                "location": "engine/runtime/pi_agents.go:180-190",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "unlinkPackageAgents enumerates the agents from the built package's agents/ directory. If that directory is already gone (for example, the user deleted the package or a rebuild failed), Uninstall reports an error and removes no links. The old unlinkGaduAgent used a fixed name and removed a stale overlay-owned GADU.md link even then. Dangling ~/.pi/agent/agents/*.md symlinks now stay behind. The same applies to links of agents later dropped from the package. This is a narrow regression in uninstall cleanup, not a blocker.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/runtime/pi_agents.go:180-190",
                  "engine/runtime/pi_gadu.go:1"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Read all 30 manifest paths in the patch.",
              "Install, Status and Uninstall continue past a per-agent conflict or frontmatter failure. Nothing is overwritten, and each failure is reported by name.",
