                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/runtime/pi_agents.go:158-172",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "unlinkPackageAgents enumerates the links from the package's agents/ directory. If that directory is gone (package already removed or never built), Uninstall appends an 'agents link: the package agents cannot be read' error note and removes no links. Any dangling ~/.pi/agent/agents/*.md symlinks the overlay created stay behind. The baseline unlinkGaduAgent removed a stale GADU.md link in this case. The same applies to a role agent dropped from a later package build: its old link is never cleaned up. Uninstall also now has no test for the missing-package case.",
                "proof_refs": [
